@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# ST7735 portability probe
+
+This is an experiment on branch `codex/portable-display-proof`, based on upstream
+FPMS commit `8beeba40a0f9d4f8045ac556a5b0780a1ce9028e`. It is not the complete
+cmprovision menu or a replacement Debian package.
+
+The ST7735 driver no longer imports the application's `constants.py`. GPIO header
+discovery is shared through a small module without WLAN Pi files, commands,
+fonts, cwd changes or network services. `EnvUtils.get_gpiochip()` remains as a
+compatible entry point for the existing application.
+
+Runtime packages for the hardware probe: `python3`, `python3-pil`,
+`python3-libgpiod`, `python3-spidev`. `python3-pytest` and `python3-qrcode` are test
+dependencies (the existing EnvUtils regression tests import qrcode).
+
+## Test environment
+
+Use a new, disposable rootfs, for example:
+
+```sh
+sudo unshare --mount --propagation private debootstrap \
+  --variant=minbase --force-check-sig \
+  --include=python3,python3-pil,python3-libgpiod,python3-spidev,python3-pytest,python3-qrcode \
+  trixie /var/lib/cmprovision-lab/trixie-portable http://deb.debian.org/debian
+```
+
+Run the tests with the source tree mounted read-only in a private mount and PID
+namespace. No host disks or host `/run` are exposed. Sysfs is read-only; libgpiod
+uses it to validate GPIO character devices.
+
+```sh
+sudo sh tools/run-portable-rootfs.sh test /var/lib/cmprovision-lab/trixie-portable "$PWD"
+```
+
+The test checks the clean OS, absence of WLAN Pi packages and identity/state
+files, import isolation and existing GPIO-chip selection regressions. It writes
+a sample frame to `ROOT/tmp/portable-preview.png`.
+
+## Bounded physical test
+
+This test is for a Waveshare 1.44-inch ST7735 HAT with its documented button
+pinout. It does not establish compatibility with every panel or carrier board.
+
+```sh
+sudo sh tools/run-portable-rootfs.sh probe /var/lib/cmprovision-lab/trixie-portable "$PWD"
+```
+
+The runner temporarily stops `wlanpi-fpms` if it was active, then draws a test
+page for 180 seconds and records GPIO input. Press all five joystick positions
+and the three side buttons. The original service is restored on exit; a separate
+systemd timer provides a fallback if the runner is killed. Other SPI/GPIO owners
+must be dealt with explicitly; this probe does not stop unrelated services.
+
+The report is `ROOT/tmp/portable-display-report.json`. Count the distinct button
+names, not just the total event count. A user's visual confirmation is still
+needed: successful SPI writes do not prove that the panel is physically visible
+or correctly oriented.
+
+The kernel remains the host kernel. Passing this test establishes clean Debian
+Trixie userspace plus real hardware access, **not** a cold boot or full acceptance
+of Raspberry Pi OS Lite. Those require booting a clean target image later.
